{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms","id":1561065,"title":"Rocket Launcher and Explosives Firearms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-27T17:59:04-07:00","id":1561065,"title":"Rocket Launcher and Explosives Firearms","content":"The table about heavy firearms give 12 to 16 damage to the rocket launcher, wich is already powerful when you add these to your success, but the little 12 notes say to look at the explosives table. This one give various stats for explosives but nothing about rocket laucncher, or maybe the closest thing: small rocket with 10 to 15 damage.<br /> <br /> What does that mean? When you shoot with the rocket laucnher you get you first damage with you success (minus the first) + the rocket launcher damage + the rocket damage?<br /> I know that it's supposed to be powerfull but still... And the book also give you the 105 and 120mm canon from tank, their shell are explosives too but this time there's nothing in the explosives table that can help figure this out<br /> <br /> Any advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T20:22:51-07:00","id":1561066,"title":"","content":"Explosives are covered on pgs 437-438. Basically, no, you don't add extra attack successes to the damage. They're just there to put its ground zero point where the attacker wants it to be. Other games usually have a Scatter mechanic to cover this; basically, the launch system has some inherent instability that put it a random number of movement measurements off-center, and each success removes one from the hex, square or what have you that it's off-target, as determined by a simple die roll where you just take the number, like with Initiative value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T04:22:03-07:00","id":1561074,"title":"","content":"But you do add the explosive damage to the weapon damage? Because if that's the case then the explosive table is incomplete or inaccurate since it's missing 105 and 120mm shells, and isn't precise when it come to &quot;small rockets&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T08:24:29-07:00","id":1561077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561074#post1561074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you do add the explosive damage to the weapon damage? Because if that's the case then the explosive table is incomplete or inaccurate since it's missing 105 and 120mm shells, and isn't precise when it come to &quot;small rockets&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> The weapon table is for the shot: is you hit the shot, you use its damage.<br /> <br /> But since the rocket is an explosive, it will explode <b>and damage what's around.</b><br /> <br /> In this case, the explosive table is to cover <b>everything it didn't hit, but are still in explosion range.<br /> <br /> <u>DO NOT ADD THEM.</u></b><br /> <br /> Use only one. The explosion is relevant for what's around the place it hit. That's why the weapon table has a bigger damage already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T13:35:58-07:00","id":1561086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561074#post1561074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you do add the explosive damage to the weapon damage? Because if that's the case then the explosive table is incomplete or inaccurate since it's missing 105 and 120mm shells, and isn't precise when it come to &quot;small rockets&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Tank cannon shells (the 105mm and 120mm) are usually either HEAT rounds that direct their explosive power to deform the casing and turn it into a narrow jet of molten metal moving in the direction of the shot at Mach 25, or solid rounds that don't explode as such. As such, they wouldn't behave like explosives on the relevant table, so there wouldn't be a reason for them to be on the explosives table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T13:39:33-07:00","id":1561088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561086#post1561086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tank cannon shells (the 105mm and 120mm) are usually either HEAT rounds that direct their explosive power to deform the casing and turn it into a narrow jet of molten metal moving in the direction of the shot at Mach 25, or solid rounds that don't explode as such. As such, they wouldn't behave like explosives on the relevant table, so there wouldn't be a reason for them to be on the explosives table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also important. Artillery usually don't use actual explosives, but enough force to be in the most interesting side of things. Even then, not enough to use explosion rules since they still rely on hitting the target, not on detonating a payload nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T01:08:53-07:00","id":1561095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561088#post1561088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also important. Artillery usually don't use actual explosives, but enough force to be in the most interesting side of things. Even then, not enough to use explosion rules since they still rely on hitting the target, not on detonating a payload nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cannons, sure. Mortars and howitzers, however, tend to be overwhelmingly vehicles for hurling large masses of high explosives at lower velocity. If they aren't doing that, they're providing smoke cover or flare illumination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T04:04:40-07:00","id":1561096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561095#post1561095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cannons, sure. Mortars and howitzers, however, tend to be overwhelmingly vehicles for hurling large masses of high explosives at lower velocity. If they aren't doing that, they're providing smoke cover or flare illumination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why &quot;usually&quot;, though I may be better saying that artillery distinguishes between &quot;large guns&quot; and &quot;large launchers&quot;.<br /> <br /> When shells have explosive effects, this is usually complicated physics and reliant on hitting the target, the explosion is secondary.<br /> <br /> Large launchers will hurl actual bombs, but they're not trying to be much of a gun and more of an improved trebuchet, hitting target with force is less important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T01:02:45-07:00","id":1561117,"title":"","content":"There needs to be a central WoD Armory/Martial Arts book with all the weapon and fighting rules in one place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T07:15:51-07:00","id":1561135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561117#post1561117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There needs to be a central WoD Armory/Martial Arts book with all the weapon and fighting rules in one place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, especially for Mage that use Tech magic and Werewolf that can face those weapons when fighting Pentex's forces.<br /> <br /> There's still some strange stats, like the .50 machine gun dealing 16 damage and the 105mm canon dealing 20. Only 4 dice of difference? I'm no expert in weaponery but that feel a bit weak for a tank weapon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T08:22:06-07:00","id":1561137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1561065-rocket-launcher-and-explosives-firearms?p=1561135#post1561135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's still some strange stats, like the .50 machine gun dealing 16 damage and the 105mm canon dealing 20. Only 4 dice of difference? I'm no expert in weaponery but that feel a bit weak for a tank weapon</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's not what the dice measure. A log - like progression is expected.<br /> <br /> What the system models isn't the joules or newtons of impact, it's the likelihood that it will impair or kill the target. Especially, in this system, a humanoid supernatural target.<br /> <br /> The 4 dice of difference means 4 dice more of effects a supernatural creature must amass on the absorption roll to survive. For Vampires, this jump from 8 Lethal average to 10 Lethal average means going from needing Stamina 4/5 to have a reasonable chance of not filling up on Bashing, to needing 8/9, which means you need both Fortitude and Stamina at high levels to deal with that. You change the kind of character that can take on it significantly.<br /> <br /> Even for &quot;realism&quot; there are several reasons for us to be entering the domain of the Law of Diminishing Returns. Usually the more you break, the more energy you would have needed to break even more at first. You're increasing power, but the outcome is also increasing everything that makes the result less predictable. Against things you kill, they're not getting deader, but against things you don't, you need way more to get a meaningful advantage.<br /> <br /> Finally, bloat usually makes the math go in weirder ways rather than realistic ways. The less dice you have to throw for something, the better it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T10:10:44-07:00","id":1561139,"title":"","content":"I don't think that 12.7mm should be doing 16 dice of damage, personally, nor the 7.62mm doing 12. More like 10 and 12, respectively. 16 is where I'd expect something a good deal larger. 16 dice is threatening the sides of some tanks, which you normally need at least 30mm to do. For that matter, 105mm and 120mm being separated by 10 dice is also... weird. These systems were originally eyeballed back in 1993 and need serious re-evaluation. Establishing some degree of armor piercing would probably go a long way toward keeping some of the direct fire weapons' damage down (not the HEAT rounds, though; getting hit by a jet of molten metal moving at Mach 25 is going to be a no good, terrible day unless you're a nova with durability scale 6).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}